Yes! I finally did it! I ascended Mase the Samurai! First time I've 
actually laid my hands on the Amulet, too.

Overall, though, I have to say luck was heavily on my side: Found three 
wands of wishing in all, the first one on Sokoban (which also gave me 
"oR), the second was the castle wand and the third I found in Yeenoghu's 
lair as I was on my way up to buy some protection. Oh, plus a throne wish.
Also, a co-aligned altar with priest pretty far down the dungeon proved 
pretty useful, as did the three or four other altars scattered around 
the post-quest levels. Oh, I found a figurune of an Angel in the castle, 
which was cool, but lost the damn thing on the Valley of the Dead as I 
couldn't be bothered to make it keep up with me.
And the altar I first visited (Famine's, chose it at random) proved to 
be lawful, so that was a bit of luck as well.
Never did find Luidos, though.

The Wizard came back to bug me three times, which, from what I hear from 
the rest of you, was pretty good, and I encountered the mysterious 
dragging force on Gehennom about six or seven times. No idea whether 
this is standard or not.

I think the extra /oW were the RNG's way of apologizing to me for my 
last death (Fully ascension-kitted valkyrie, died to a trickery just 
after slaying Asmodeus), which I feel is only fair. I think one wand 
would've done it, though, and I'm afraid I'll be paying for the extra 
for many games to come.

